00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.269
Number 5 - Derek is Losing his powers

00:00:47.269 --> 00:00:51.590
They still haven't explained what it is that
Kate took other than to say it's his "True

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:55.820
Essence". The way I'm thinking about it in
my head is that she just took his Wolf Mojo.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.239
Like the wolf part of his soul. I have a few
theories about why that is, mostly involving

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:02.940
a lot of double crosses and the true identity
of the benefactor.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.330
I think based on Derek's progression, his
Wolf Tank will be empty way before the season

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:11.680
finale. Like he'll be a normal person sometime
in the next 4 episodes. What would he even

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.710
do with himself then? He'd have to get a real
job, especially if they can't get their families

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.390
money back. And he'd be extra vulnerable to
attack.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:20.830
I think it's more likely that he would team
up with Chris Argent and try to Hunt down

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.810
supernatural creatures and help them, rather
than kill them like the Calaveras. It would

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.180
be like the Winchester Brothers Teen Wolf
Edition.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.030
If they made a spin off like that, would you
guys watch it?

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.570
Number 4 - Lydia and Malia decode the next
part of the list

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:37.490
Did anyone else feel like they totally reversed
roles. Like Malia was the one flipping out

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.770
last week and Lydia was the voice of reason,
and this week Lydia completely lost her mind

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:45.660
staring at that record player all weekend
and Malia was the normal one.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.470
On top of that, does anyone notice that each
episode Malia is starting to look more and

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:55.140
more like a normal teenage girl. Like fixing
her hair and wearing makeup, some of her reactions

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.030
were still very much coyote adorable. Like
almost resting her head on Lydia's shoulder

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.490
in the art studio.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.650
Anyone who has owned a big dog will understand.
They stand behind you when you're sitting

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:07.750
down and just stick their heads out right
in your face. It's pretty funny.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.959
The real WTF came later when Lydia lost it
all over Meredith. Pretty much everyone in

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:15.379
the episode was an IED just waiting to explode.

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:19.790
Number 3 - Everyone Is An Improvised Explosive
Device

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.730
That's what IED stands for in case you weren't
sure. In the episode they were using it as

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.659
a metaphor for Liam's Intermittent Explosive
Disorder. But when you hear someone say IED,

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:31.769
they're usually referring to a dirty bomb.
A dirty bomb is typically something you find

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:35.299
in overseas urban combat. Like the Iraq war
or Afghanistan.

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:39.909
So the idea of a bomb going off informed all
the different plot points as well as the character

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:44.969
arcs. Of all the episodes so far I feel like
the writing in this one was the best. The

00:02:44.969 --> 00:02:49.239
more you can tie things in the episode to
the main theme, the stronger the whole episode

00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:51.540
is.
Like Lydia blowing up in Meredith's face,

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:56.140
Garrett blowing up on the lacrosse field or
Liam blowing up in everyone's face.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.370
The problem is that not all of those explosive
devices or people can be cured with Anti Psychotic

00:02:59.370 --> 00:02:59.689
meds.

00:02:59.689 --> 00:03:04.420
I love how Parrish kind of became the Jeremy
Renner character from Hurt Locker. Fun Fact:

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.859
That was the part that got Jeremy Renner hired
as Hawkeye in all the Marvel films.

00:03:08.859 --> 00:03:13.349
Parrish is a whole other story, but a big
part of the IED plot was disarming the people

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:17.540
bombs. Parrish kind of disarmed Lydia but
the real callback was Scott and Stiles throwing

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.609
Liam in the shower. That's a nice callback
to Scott getting thrown in the shower when

00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:25.909
he first started freaking out in season 1
and in the flashback where Peter threw Derek

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:28.849
in the shower after the basketball game when
he was a freshman.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:31.920
The big thing we learn from this I think is
that none of the male characters are allowed

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.779
to be normal in the locker room. It's like
it's a requirement they have a freakout in

00:03:35.779 --> 00:03:36.150
there.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.409
Number 2 - CSI Teen Wolf

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:43.180
Tyler Posey was talking about the CSI style
scenes Stiles had saying that their editor,

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:48.129
the person who edits Teen Wolf used to edit
for CSI. And they have a very particular way

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:53.739
they cut the scenes when characters are figuring
out clues. So they called Stiles scenes CSI

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:54.209
Teen Wolf.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:58.590
First off, the scenes looked beautiful from
a cinematography perspective, but two did

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.889
you notice all the red tape Stiles was using?
It was a nice callback to all his red markers

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:06.279
from season 3 and Malia's Red Markers this
season.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:10.870
At this point I feel like Red has become the
color for WTF on the show. Anytime there's

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:14.980
a freakout or you're talking about murder
or something awful is happening, the color

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.019
red is invoked either visually or metaphorically.

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:21.270
For instance, the deadpool chart, full of
red, Lydia's freaky record player, Red. And

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:25.520
anytime Scott loses his shit on someone his
eyes glow alpha Red.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.640
Keep your eyes peeled for Red in next week's
episode. I'll bet that anytime something crazy

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.970
happens, red will be somewhere in the frame.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:35.320
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - Parrish is On
The List

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.810
I think we all kind of suspected something
was up with him. He's always been waay too

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:43.210
cool about Lydia's supernatural status and
all the crazy Beacon Hills stuff that has

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:43.760
happened.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.550
Just because he's on the list doesn't guarantee
he's a Werewolf, but what else do you think

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:51.890
he could be? The show has opened up the mythology
a lot every year. So it's possible he could

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.190
be something we haven't seen yet.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:58.340
Kira is a Thunder Kitsune and can absorb electrical
energy, if Parrish did Bomb Disposal during

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.310
the war in Afghanistan, maybe his abilities
have something to do with absorbing damage

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.910
or seeing how things work?

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:08.850
If you had a supernatural ability to look
for clues, becoming a deputy sheriff would

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:15.180
be an appropriate career path. He said he
was drawn to beacon hills, so maybe he's a

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:19.220
banshee too and just has a WTF radar like
Lydia.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.610
I think the show is 'shipping him with Lydia
anyway, so I'll bet he joins the pack unofficially

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:26.870
by the end of the season, if he survives.
Which I hope he does. I like him a lot more

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.060
this season.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:31.520
And it wasn't one of my favorites, but the
Calaveras showing up at the end got me thinking

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.310
about who the Benefactor might be. They said
that Braeden had gone missing, she was looking

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.420
for Kate, but what if she's in on the Deadpool
plot.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:47.420
I thought that Peter might be behind it all,
or at least the Kate part. Using it secretly

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:53.560
as a way to steal Derek's power. I could see
him sacrificing all that money and letting

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:58.140
all those people die just to get his Alpha
powers back. But that seems a little too complicated.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.810
I find that the real solutions tend to be
a lot simpler. But the benefactor knew that

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:08.600
Liam had just been turned into a werewolf.
And it has to be someone who knew Aiden and

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.820
Allison. I'm starting to think it's someone
who's inside the pack or was in the pack.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:17.170
That technically includes Peter and Braeden
but it could also include Ethan and Isaac

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.030
who we haven't seen yet this season.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:23.810
So if you want to theorycraft, just keep it
to people close to the pack. You remember

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.470
that old saying that most robberies are 'inside
jobs'.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:31.420
My craziest theory is that it's Parrish. He
has knowledge of explosives, like the one

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.310
that disarmed Kate and Derek in the vault.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.040
But let me know what your theories are?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.100
I wouldn't be surprised to learn that Peter
or Parrish were working with Kate or Braeden.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.970
Those four characters are like the highest
on my watch list.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:46.480
Overall the episode was a solid B plus, I
felt like there were two clear parts to the

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.680
story. There was pre-lacrosse, then Lacrosse.
Everything before lacrosse was finding out

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.230
where the IED bomb was, represented by Garrett.
Once they found out where he was, the Lacrosse

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.380
half of the episode began and it was all about
them waiting for the bomb to go off. The wolfsbane

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:57.440
bomb.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.090
You could even make it simpler than that.
It was like the whole episode was about finding

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:05.590
a bunch of different bombs and disarming them.
Sometimes those bombs were people inside the

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:09.300
pack, sometimes they were other people like
Garrett and Violet and sometimes they were

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:12.530
actual bombs, like Parrish in the flashback.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:17.270
The other real points of interest was the
talk going on around the episode, Jeff Davis

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.670
took over the Teen Wolf twitter account and
Tyler posey and the rest of the cast were

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.760
live tweeting funny stuff while it was happening.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:26.110
Tyler's favorite Derek Scott moment ever was
when Derek was congratulating him in the locker

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:30.780
room. And Jeff Davis posted a picture of them
making Stiles opening title sequence scene.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.060
With all the red tape. This is what it looks
like when they're shooting it. Isn't that

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:37.700
crazy. All that time for just a few seconds
of footage.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:42.640
The last big about the episode I'll say is
that the last name on the list, the one they

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.740
have to unlock. it's probably someone who
was in the pack but has died. That could be

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:52.150
Jackson, or any of the dead Hale's. It seems
like it's all a vendetta killing in reaction

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.530
to the deaths of those keyword characters,
like Allison and Aiden.

